State
      The minimal information required to continue computation correctly.

A single state can involve
      multiple variables
      a data structure
      or even an invariant

Story-based coding 
          is fragile 
              because variables represent temporary thoughts that keep changing during the loop.
State-based coding 
          is stable 
              because variables represent invariants — fixed truths about the system

Example
        Traffic Light
              Story
                    If it was green for 30 seconds, turn yellow… unless an emergency vehicle passed
                    This quickly becomes messy and buggy

              State
                    State Space
                          RED, YELLOW, GREEN
                          
                    Transitions
                          RED → GREEN
                          GREEN → YELLOW
                          YELLOW → RED

                  Now the system is bounded and predictable

        
